::TF_Gravity::Gravity causes objects to fall toward Earth.{T ####General feedback\: Correct — 9.8 m/s^2 near sea level.}

// 2. MULTIPLE-CHOICE (single correct)
::MC_Spectrum::Which colour lies between green and orange in the visible spectrum?
{
=yellow #Yes, roughly 565–590 nm.
~blue   #Too short a wavelength.
~red    #Too long a wavelength.
~violet #Way off.
}

// 3. MULTIPLE-ANSWER (partial credit)
::MC_PrimesU10::Select all prime numbers below 10.
{
~%25% 2   #Prime
~%25% 3   #Prime
~%25% 5   #Prime
~%25% 7   #Prime
~%-25% 4  #Composite
~%-25% 6  #Composite
~%-25% 8  #Composite
~%-25% 9  #Composite
}

// 4. SHORT ANSWER (fill-in-blank)
::SA_Water::What is the chemical formula for water?{ =H2O =h2o ~H20 #Careful\: that’s twenty not two! }

// 5. NUMERICAL (tolerance)
::NUM_Pi::Give π rounded to two decimals (±0.01).
{ #3.14:0.01 
####π ≈ 3.14159.}

// 6. NUMERICAL (range)
::NUM_Range50to60::Enter any whole number 50–60 inclusive.
{ #50..60 }

// 7. MATCHING
::MATCH_Capitals::Match each country to its capital.
{
=France -> Paris
=Italy  -> Rome
=Spain  -> Madrid
=Germany-> Berlin
}


